# Copy to mobile/.env.local if you need to override the API URL.
# .env.local is gitignored.
#
# You normally do NOT need this file. In development the API base URL is
# derived from whatever address Metro is served on, which is the machine
# running the backend — that covers both supported setups:
#
#   npm start             phone and laptop on the same wifi
#   npm run start:tailscale   any network, via Tailscale
#
# Set this only to point the app at a deployed backend. Required for release
# builds, which have no Metro host to derive from.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://civickit.org/api

# Port used when deriving the dev URL from the Metro host. Defaults to 3000.
# Only applies when EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is unset.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_PORT=3000

# Stand in for the device's GPS during development.
#
# Two things key off where the phone physically is, and both fail closed
# outside St. Louis: the nearby-issues feed (5 mile radius) and the "outside
# our service area" bounds check, which disables issue submission. Every seed
# fixture is St. Louis, so without this a developer elsewhere sees an empty app
# and cannot tell a real bug from their own latitude.
#
# Uncomment ONE line. Ignored entirely in release builds.
#
#   midtown       inside the seeded Midtown CID geofence, near all 12 issues
#   out-of-area   deliberately outside it, to test that banner from inside STL
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_LOCATION=midtown

# For a point with no name. Both halves required; latitude first, and longitude
# is negative in the US. Wins over EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_LOCATION if both are set.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_LAT=38.6365
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_LNG=-90.2220
